  "lines": [
    {
      "id": "hook",
      "text": "Three animals that actually get drunk.",
      "hold_after": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "chimp1",
      "text": "First, chimpanzees in Guinea. Farmers tap palm trees and collect the sap, which ferments into palm wine."
    },
    {
      "id": "chimp2",
      "text": "The chimps sneak in, soak it up with leaves, and drink it. Some drank so much they had to lie down for a nap."
    },
    {
      "id": "moose1",
      "text": "Next, a moose in Sweden. It ate so many fermented apples, it got stuck in an apple tree."
    },
    {
      "id": "moose2",
      "text": "Rescuers had to come and cut it free."
    },
    {
      "id": "wax1",
      "text": "Finally, Bohemian waxwings. These birds eat fermented berries and crash into windows."
    },
    {
      "id": "wax2",
      "text": "In Canada, wildlife officers actually put the drunk birds in little cages until they sobered up."
    },
    {
      "id": "wax3",
      "text": "A drunk tank. For birds."
    }
  ]
}
